{
  "_note": "web.* feeds apps/game/web/pixl.css. godot.* feeds apps/game/theme.json. Both share the same token names on purpose, but not (yet) the same literal values: main_theme.tres and pixl.css were designed independently and were never pixel-identical, so forcing them onto one literal value per token would be a visual change, not plumbing. Unifying the actual hues is a deliberate future design pass, not this one. godot.light does not exist: the game has no light-mode design yet, so PixlTheme falls back to godot.dark whenever a synced 'light' choice reaches the game.",
